  "answer_core": "Slow the situation down and keep your child’s safety and trust at the center. Before making big moves like reporting or shutting down the phone, talk with a therapist, RAINN, or legal counsel to get grounded guidance. Coordinate with the co-parent enough to stay aligned on safety without turning it into a blame fight.\n\nUse clear tripwires for escalation: any request to meet, sexual images, threats, signs the older person is contacting other minors, your child saying they feel pressured or afraid, or the contact jumping to a hidden channel after you set boundaries. If any of these appear, move quickly to cut off contact and seek professional or legal support.\n\nIf nothing hits a tripwire yet, avoid sudden device shutdowns that could push the contact underground. A quiet or monitored phone is weak reassurance by itself; it may simply mean the channel moved. Stay present, keep communication open with your child, and check in regularly while a professional helps you plan next steps.",
